## Whole-file declarations, data, registration and contextual obligations (unit-1)

Declares itanium and itanic as aliases for the ia64 architecture. ArchInfo reads the aliases block; InfoObject derives the canonical name ia64 from this filename. canon_processor normalizes input to lowercase, removes spaces and trademark markers, and returns ia64 when the normalized CPU matches either alias. canonicalize_options writes that result to options.arch and raises UserError when no architecture matches. The file contains no executable body, ISA extension entries, promise, listener, or cleanup action. Changing either alias affects accepted Botan CPU inputs and the known-CPU list.


